  "id": "waardenburgs-syndrome",
  "term": "Waardenburg’s syndrome",
  "definition": "Waardenburg’s syndrome is a rare inherited condition, usually passed in an autosomal dominant pattern, with several forms and variable expression. It can involve changes in pigmentation of the hair, skin, or eyes, congenital deafness, and distinctive facial features, and it may result from abnormal development of neural crest cells.",
